@title Clickstream data platform
@subtitle Data Engineering · Harbor Media · as of 2026-09-30

# Overview

We collect about 1,800 million events per day from our apps and land them in a lake that analysts query.

# Architecture diagram

diagram clicks dir=LR title="Clickstream data platform"
clicks: web "Web and Mobile Apps" ext
clicks: kstream "Clickstream Stream" queue "Kinesis"
clicks: fh "Firehose" svc
clicks: raw "Raw Bucket" store "S3"
clicks: curated "Curated Bucket" store "S3"
clicks: glue "Glue Catalog" store
clicks: emr "EMR Cluster" svc
clicks: rs "Redshift Cluster" db "ra3.4xlarge"
clicks: superset "Superset" ext
clicks: fs "Feature Store" store
clicks: web -> kstream : events
clicks: kstream -> fh : batch
clicks: fh -> raw : parquet every 5 min
clicks: raw -> emr : nightly ETL
clicks: emr -> curated : cleaned tables
clicks: curated -> rs : COPY
clicks: glue -> emr : schemas
clicks: rs -> superset : SQL
clicks: emr -> fs : features
clicks: group lake "Lake VPC 10.40.0.0/16" emr, rs, fs
clicks: group analytics "Analytics account" raw, curated, glue, lake
clicks: group ingest "Ingest account" kstream, fh

# Datasets

table = Dataset,Daily volume (GB),Retention (days),Owner; raw_events,940,30,Ingest squad; sessions,120,400,Analytics Eng; page_views,310,400,Analytics Eng; ad_impressions,260,90,Ad Tech

# Known limits

- Firehose buffering means data arrives up to 5 minutes late.
- The nightly ETL finishes around 03:40 UTC.
- Redshift is a 4-node ra3.4xlarge cluster. It queues queries above 50 concurrent users.
